# SITL: turn GPS truly OFF (Phase 3 — the real indoor case).
#
# TARGET FIRMWARE: ArduCopter 4.6.x (matches our real FlywooF745 on 4.6.3).
#
# Load AFTER sitl_flow_phaseA.parm and sitl_flow_phaseB.parm (each + reboot), then
# reboot once more:
#   param load /Users/danieleamore/Studium/Drohnen-mit-KI/Pi-Code/params/sitl_gps_off.parm
#   reboot
#
# With GPS off, nothing seeds the EKF origin any more — the companion must send
# SET_GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN itself (config.set_origin_on_start = True, see Drone.set_origin).
#
# ARMING_CHECK is the bitmask from ArduPilot's own copter-optflow.parm at tag
# Copter-4.6.3: everything enabled EXCEPT the GPS-lock check (bit 3), the parameter
# check (bit 5) and visual odometry (bit 18). Without clearing the GPS bit, arming is
# refused indoors even though optical flow provides a perfectly good relative position.
#
# NOTE: the SITL compass is modelled at the simulator's home position. Start SITL at the
# SAME place as config.origin_lat/lon or pre-arm fails with "Check mag field":
#   sim_vehicle.py -v ArduCopter --console --custom-location=50.131196,8.692972,112,0
GPS1_TYPE 0
ARMING_CHECK 786390
